We need to ensure children structure: root molecule with children reactions? In example, root mol has children list containing reaction node(s). Reaction node has children list of precursor molecules. In our route, we have two steps sequentially. Typically tree: target mol -> reaction (sulfonylation) -> precursor aniline + TsCl. The aniline node then has its own reaction (amide coupling) -> precursors 4-aminocinnamic acid and p-phenylenediamine. So hierarchical.

Thus JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)Nc3ccccc3N)cc2)cc1",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id": "sulfonamide_formation",
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"ClS(=O)(=O)c1ccc(C)cc1"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Nc1ccc(/C=C/C(=O)Nc2ccccc2N)cc1"} // intermediate aniline
     ]
   }
 ]
}

But need to embed second reaction under intermediate aniline. So intermediate aniline node will have its own children reaction.

Thus:

{
